# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings: LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) checks source out as CRLF. Nothing in
# this repository wants that: the AD-16 header-provenance tests compare port
# markers byte-for-byte, and several extraction regexes match on \n. CI runs on
# Linux and so never sees CRLF, which is exactly why this went unnoticed --
# a fresh Windows clone failed 43 tests, including the licence-header gate that
# CLAUDE.md makes a hard requirement, while CI stayed green.
#
# Ten stories never hit it because agents WRITE files (LF stays LF on disk);
# autocrlf converts on CHECKOUT, so the first real checkout was the epic merge.
# Field case: Epic 1 retrospective 2026-08-30, Finding 1.
#
# This line must stay FIRST -- later rules override it per-path.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries are never line-ending converted or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.pyc binary

# Deferred-work ledger is append-only across parallel epic branches
_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/deferred-work.md merge=union

# Cycle logs are TAB-delimited and parsed field-by-field on resume; a CRLF checkout
# would append \r to every metadata value. Keep the tracker files LF in the working
# tree too, so every epic worktree parses identically.
# (Redundant under the blanket rule above, kept because they document why.)
_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/*.md eol=lf
_bmad-output/implementation-artifacts/*.yaml eol=lf
_bmad/custom/*.yaml eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF: core.autocrlf=true would otherwise give a fresh
# clone CRLF shebangs, which Git Bash rejects with "bad interpreter".
*.sh eol=lf

# Golden replay fixtures are hashed and diffed byte-for-byte across engines;
# a CRLF checkout on a fresh clone (core.autocrlf=true) would corrupt that
# comparison. Every downstream reader already normalises line endings as a
# workaround -- this makes the LF guarantee structural instead.
test/replays/** eol=lf

# The spine's append-only decision log; ARCHITECTURE-SPINE.md itself is NOT
# union-merged -- its conflicts are reconciled deterministically at SC-4-P.
_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/architecture/**/.memlog.md merge=union
